  ('Receptionist', 'GB', "Of course. A bug hotel is a kind of shelter that gives insects and other small creatures somewhere to live, especially over the winter. Each child builds their own small one, using a wooden frame, which we provide. They fill it with natural materials. We use pine cones, dry leaves, pieces of bark and hollow bamboo canes. Solitary bees, for example, like to lay their eggs inside the bamboo tubes, and ladybirds often spend the winter hidden among the pine cones."),
